the SQL process,","+//! not an OS PID), as exposed by `connection_id()` and `system.processes.id`.","+//! HTTP login/client-session ids and MySQL numeric protocol ids are unchanged;","+//! temporary-table keys and logs treat internal session ids as opaque strings.","+//! Client query ids may use any prefix, including `p-`; there is no reserved","+//! query-id namespace. Hex, UUID and UUID-plus-sequence ids remain supported.","+//!","+//! `KillTarget` resolves a node-local MySQL `u32` connection id first. For","+//! KILL QUERY, `p-` ids prefer a session match and fall back to query lookup;","+//! other strings prefer a query match and fall back to a legacy session id.","+//! The prefix is only a lookup-order hint. If both kinds exist on a node, the","+//! preferred match wins. Only absence triggers the alternate identifier lookup:","+//! denial or a failed conditional cancellation never tries the other kind.","+//! Numeric query ids that parse as `u32` retain connection-id semantics.","+//! KILL CONNECTION looks up sessions regardless of prefix. Authorized query-only","+//! matches return `BadArguments` rather than disconnecting their sessions.","+//!","+//! Lookup is scoped to the requester's tenant, including before identifier","+//! fallback and query-only CONNECTION errors. Other tenants' sessions and queries","+//! count as absent, so their ids cannot hide a match in the requester's tenant.","+//! Lookup includes queued queries but excludes FlightRPC fragment sessions,","+//! which are not registered as active client sessions. A local in-tenant match","+//! stops the search; otherwise warehouse peers are searched until one matches.","+//! Numeric MySQL connection ids are never forwarded.","+//!","+//! # Authorization and cancellation","+//!","+//! Requester identity requires a nonempty matching tenant, even for SUPER.","+//! Within that tenant, ownership compares username and hostname; other targets,","+//! including userless sessions, require global SUPER (including role grants).","+//! Duplicate query IDs are resolved among in-tenant candidates by choosing an","+//! authorized session. If none is authorized, the query match still denies KILL;","+//! it does not fall back to a sid or a peer.","+//! Authorization precedes queue removal and cancellation. Same-tenant denial","+//! returns `PermissionDenied` (1063); missing and cross-tenant targets both return","+//! `UnknownSession` (1053). This exposes existence only within the same tenant,","+//! including beyond rows visible to the caller in `system.processes`.","+//! Ordinary client sessions use the configured tenant; runtime tenant overrides","+//! are restricted to management/sandbox modes and internal Local sessions.","+//!","+//! Query-id cancellation checks and pins the matching context under the session's","+//! context-slot lock. Queue entries and semaphore acquirers use an immutable UUID","+//! from that shared context, not the client query ID. Removal after releasing the","+//! lock cannot touch another request reusing that ID, even on the same session.","+//! Only that pinned context is canceled, never the connection's next statement.","+//!","+//! # Flight and rolling upgrades","+//!","+//! SUPER retains the legacy action, with upgraded senders appending optional","+//! requester access fields to the unchanged top-level plan fields. Upgraded","+//! receivers check that tenant; old receivers ignore the extra fields. Trusted","+//! old requests without access fields are limited to the receiver's configured","+//! tenant, not a wildcard. Their actual requester tenant cannot be recovered:","+//! identity-less old senders and old receivers remain an isolation limitation.","+//!","+//! Non-SUPER uses only `/actions/kill_query_v2`, carrying tenant, user identity","+//! and SUPER status. Unsupported v2 is treated as not found, with no legacy","+//! fallback. Old coordinators cannot resolve query-id KILL; use their actual","+//! session ids subject to the old node's privilege requirements.","+//!","+//! # HTTP query lifecycle","+//!","+//! SQL KILL does not call or change the HTTP query-kill endpoint. After stopping,","+//! `/page` and `/final` return normal HTTP 200 envelopes with `Failed` and","+//! `AbortedQuery` (1043). Query/session/MySQL-id KILL QUERY and explicit queue","+//! removal use `Query canceled by KILL`. KILL CONNECTION also closes a queued","+//! session after removal; other connection-kill/shutdown errors retain their semantics.","+//! Buffered rows do not make failure succeed; the query-log event is `Aborted`.","+//! Clients still finalize results: finalization","+//! decrements the active count, and HttpQueryManager removes retained records","+//! after its existing timeout. The HTTP `/kill` closed-query response is unchanged.","+"," use std::collections::HashMap;"," use std::sync::Arc;"," "," use databend_common_exception::ErrorCode;"," use databend_common_exception::Result;","+use databend_common_meta_app::principal::GrantObject;","+use databend_common_meta_app::principal::UserIdentity;","+use databend_common_meta_app::principal::UserPrivilegeType;"," use databend_common_sql::plans::KillPlan;","+use serde::Deserialize;","+use serde::Serialize;"," "," use crate::clusters::ClusterHelper;"," use crate::clusters::FlightParams;"," use crate::interpreters::Interpreter;"," use crate::pipelines::PipelineBuildResult;"," use crate::servers::flight::v1::actions::KILL_QUERY;","+use crate::servers::flight::v1::actions::KILL_QUERY_V2;","+use crate::servers::flight::v1::actions::KillQueryRequest;","+use crate::servers::flight::v1::actions::LegacyKillQueryRequest;","+use crate::sessions::INTERNAL_SESSION_ID_PREFIX;"," use crate::sessions::QueriesQueueManager;"," use crate::sessions::QueryContext;","+use crate::sessions::Session;","+use crate::sessions::SessionManager;"," use crate::sessions::TableContextCluster;"," use crate::sessions::TableContextSettings;"," ","+/// Authorization captured on the requesting node and carrie